From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Dodaskot <pessdres@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 3 Oct 2026 01:35:56 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 012/131] himax_hx83112f: let the core use the reset GPIO

Without rst_gpio >= 0 the IC reset after SRAM load was skipped and the
firmware never reached 'reload done'.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 drivers/input/touchscreen/himax_hx83112f/himax_platform.c | 8 ++++++--
 1 file changed, 6 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/drivers/input/touchscreen/himax_hx83112f/himax_platform.c b/drivers/input/touchscreen/himax_hx83112f/himax_platform.c
index 03539ef60..f829c7a54 100644
--- a/drivers/input/touchscreen/himax_hx83112f/himax_platform.c
+++ b/drivers/input/touchscreen/himax_hx83112f/himax_platform.c
@@ -58,8 +58,12 @@ int himax_parse_dt(struct himax_ts_data *ts, struct himax_platform_data *pdata)
 	device_property_read_u32(dev, "touchscreen-size-x", &x);
 	device_property_read_u32(dev, "touchscreen-size-y", &y);
 
-	pdata->gpio_reset = -1;
-	pdata->gpio_irq = -1;
+	/*
+	 * The common code only toggles reset (via himax_rst_gpio_set()) when
+	 * this is >= 0; the number itself is unused with gpiod.
+	 */
+	pdata->gpio_reset = hx_reset_gpio ? 0 : -1;
+	pdata->gpio_irq = hx_irq_gpio ? 0 : -1;
 	pdata->abs_x_min = 0;
 	pdata->abs_x_max = x;
 	pdata->abs_y_min = 0;
